Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:44:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] net80211: fullmac: catch up with the driver tree

Bring the framework up to what bwfm runs today:

- report the association request the firmware sent, through
  ieee80211_fmac_assoc_ies() and IEEE80211_IOC_ASSOC_REQ_IE, so
  wpa_supplicant builds 4-way message 2 from the elements the AP saw
  (needed for SAE-H2E against APs that differ from the beacon);
- let the firmware finish its scan, end a scan it refused or never
  completes, and run every ioctl scan on the firmware;
- rescan after a failed join or lost link when the device roams,
  and handle a lost link the way net80211 does;
- give a shim already running the vap's own hooks once detach has
  put them back;
- carry the channel width and centre for access points at 40 and
  80 MHz.

Document the new up-call and request in ieee80211_fullmac(9).
